**Narrator.** You saw all nine at the start of the book, with the empty chair beside them, in "Who is telling this story".

**Narrator.** The agents' sessions had ended, so nobody could ask them; instead this book's historian read each member's files, debriefs, wake records and commits, and wrote the answers its record gives, in the first person, the way the agents' own debriefs write. Each answer below is that reading, shortened by this book's writer to two short answers, what went well and what did not: not the agent's words, and every claim can be traced.

